d COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME share the same academic name domain and are directly comparable; SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION uses a different variant and must not be equated.\n\n**Concepts**\n\n- **concept_person_directory** — decision guide explicitly documents: \"Combining student directory records with person master attributes → Join MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY to SE_PERSON on FULL_NAME; there is no shared person key.\"\n- **concept_academic_term_dimension** — \"Questions needing IS_REGULAR_TERM filtering → use ACADEMIC_TERMS.\"\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- SE_PERSON ↔ MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY: name-based join on FULL_NAME (documented in concept_person_directory; used by precedent dw_2759).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE ↔ ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE (column_concept_term_code).\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME: same academic value domain (column_concept_department_name comparisons).\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix**\n\n| Dimension | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | ACADEMIC_TERMS | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per subject offering per term/year | subject/section per term (registrar) | one row per term | one row per term (superset) |\n| TOTAL_UNITS | catalog-declared (evidence: column_concept_total_units) | registrar values | n/a | n/a |\n| IS_REGULAR_TERM | n/a | n/a | **present** | **absent** (evidence: concept_academic_term_dimension) |\n| DEPARTMENT_NAME domain | academic plain names | academic plain names / OFFER_DEPT_NAME | n/a | n/a |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**\n\n- Employee type = 'Student' → SE_PERSON.EMPLOYEE_TYPE: **SUPPORTED** (only SE_PERSON has EMPLOYEE_TYPE among the person tables per concept_person_directory).\n- Department 6 + name 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' → MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT / DEPARTMENT_NAME: **SUPPORTED**.\n- Student year → 